2c:["$","div",null,{"className":"container-luxe","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"relative aspect-3/2 w-full overflow-hidden bg-ivory-deep md:aspect-video","children":["$","$L23",null,{"src":"/images/blog/pashmina-vs-wool.png","alt":"Pashmina and handloom wool cloth laid side by side for comparison","fill":true,"priority":true,"quality":82,"sizes":"(min-width: 1600px) 100rem, 100vw","className":"object-cover"}]}]}]
2d:["$","div",null,{"className":"container-luxe max-w-[44rem] py-16","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col","children":[["$","p","paragraph-0",{"className":"mt-5 text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.75] text-mocha","children":"Both come from animals, both trap air, both are sold as winter cloth. Beyond that they are genuinely different materials, and choosing between them is mostly a question of what you want the piece to do."}],["$","h2","heading-1",{"className":"mt-14 font-serif text-[1.625rem] leading-tight text-charcoal md:text-[2rem]","children":"Diameter is the whole story"}],["$","p","paragraph-2",{"className":"mt-5 text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.75] text-mocha","children":"Sheep’s wool used in shawls runs from 19 microns (fine merino) up past 28 (handloom wool). Pashm is 12–15. That single difference produces almost every other difference between the two."}],["$","h2","heading-3",{"className":"mt-14 font-serif text-[1.625rem] leading-tight text-charcoal md:text-[2rem]","children":"Warmth and weight"}],["$","p","paragraph-4",{"className":"mt-5 text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.75] text-mocha","children":"Per gram, Pashmina is substantially warmer, because finer fibre packs more insulating air per unit of mass. In absolute terms a heavy 450-gram handloom wool shawl will still out-warm a 180-gram Pashmina one — it simply weighs two and a half times as much and looks it."}],["$","h2","heading-5",{"className":"mt-14 font-serif text-[1.625rem] leading-tight text-charcoal md:text-[2rem]","children":"Against the skin"}],["$","p","paragraph-6",{"className":"mt-5 text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.75] text-mocha","children":"Below about 16 microns, wool stops triggering the prickle response. Pashmina and fine cashmere can be worn on bare skin by nearly everyone; ordinary wool cannot."}],["$","h2","heading-7",{"className":"mt-14 font-serif text-[1.625rem] leading-tight text-charcoal md:text-[2rem]","children":"Durability"}],["$","p","paragraph-8",{"className":"mt-5 text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.75] text-mocha","children":"Here wool wins. A Kashmiri handloom wool shawl will take daily abuse for decades and improve as it softens. Pashmina wants more care: it pills more readily in its first season, snags on jewellery, and does not enjoy being sat on."}],["$","h2","heading-9",{"className":"mt-14 font-serif text-[1.625rem] leading-tight text-charcoal md:text-[2rem]","children":"Which to buy"}],["$","ul","list-10",{"className":"mt-6 flex flex-col gap-3","children":[["$","li","For evening, occasion and travel where bulk matters: pure Pashmina.",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.7] text-mocha","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":true,"className":"mt-3.5 h-px w-3.5 shrink-0 bg-gold"}],"For evening, occasion and travel where bulk matters: pure Pashmina."]}],["$","li","For daily winter wear, commuting and hard use: fine merino or Kashmiri handloom wool.",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.7] text-mocha","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":true,"className":"mt-3.5 h-px w-3.5 shrink-0 bg-gold"}],"For daily winter wear, commuting and hard use: fine merino or Kashmiri handloom wool."]}],["$","li","For a first serious piece that will be worn constantly: cashmere sits usefully between the two.",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.7] text-mocha","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":true,"className":"mt-3.5 h-px w-3.5 shrink-0 bg-gold"}],"For a first serious piece that will be worn constantly: cashmere sits usefully between the two."]}],["$","li","For gifting: Pashmina, almost always — it is the piece people keep.",{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.7] text-mocha","children":["$L32","For gifting: Pashmina, almost always — it is the piece people keep."]}]]}],"$L33"]}],null,"$L34"]}]
