ol Shawl handmade?","answer":"Yes. Every Pashmore piece is hand-spun, handwoven and hand-finished by artisan families in Kashmir. Small irregularities in the weave are the signature of handwork, not a defect."},{"question":"How do I know the Pashmina is genuine?","answer":"Each order ships with a craft certificate recording the fibre grade, the loom it was woven on and the name of the weaver who finished it."},{"question":"Can I return it if the colour is not what I expected?","answer":"Yes. Unused pieces in their original packaging can be returned within 14 days of delivery. Handwoven textiles photograph slightly differently under different light, so we make returns straightforward."}],"rating":{"average":4.6,"count":340},"relatedSlugs":"$undefined"},"sizes":"(min-width: 1280px) 30vw, (min-width: 768px) 30vw, 45vw","priority":false}],"$L36","$L37"]}]]}]
